H@L@H@!H@C+H!k1k0-H@.k:k0-H@k1k0-+.H@C+H!k{f@H@!H@C+H!k}f@H@!H@C+H!L!
H@L@H@!H@C+H!k1k0-H@.k H@k1k0-+.H@C+H!k{f@H@!H@C+H!k}f@H@!H@C+H!L!

H@
  L@      H@!       H@C+ H!
  k1k0-   H@.
  k\      H@k1k0-+. H@C+ H!
  k{f@    H@!       H@C+ H!
  H@
    kkf@  H@!       H@C+ H!
    klf@  H@!       H@C+ H!
    k:k0- H@!       H@C+ H!
    k=f@  H@!       H@C+ H!
    kjf@  H@!       H@C+ H!
          H@!       H@C+ H!
  k}f@    H@!       H@C+ H!
L!

\ Line comments are now supported!

\ C ( -- u )          Get size of cell in bytes
\ H ( -- a-addr )     Get address of here. NOTE: Should this be address-aligned?
\ L ( -- a-addr )     Get address of latest
\ @ ( a-addr -- x )   Load cell x from addr
\ $ ( c-addr -- c )   Load byte c from addr
\ ! ( x a-addr -- )   Store cell x at addr
\ . ( c c-addr -- )   Store byte c at addr
\ f ( c -- xt )       Get execution token of c
\ j ( ? -- )          Jump to address provided by next input token if ? = 0
\ J ( -- )            Jump to address provided by next input token
\ k ( -- c )          Get next byte in input
\ l ( -- x )          Push next input token as literal
\ x ( xt -- ... )     Run the execution token
\ + ( x1 x2 -- x3 )   Push x3 where x3 = x1 + x2
\ - ( x1 x2 -- x3 )   Push x3 where x3 = x1 - x2
\ = ( x1 x2 -- ? )    If x1 = x2, pushes -1, else pushes 0

\ vim:ft=forth
